{
  "schema": "zama-solana-user-decrypt-signing-message/v1",
  "description": "Literal byte vectors for the Solana user-decrypt ed25519 signing message — the hand-mirrored codec in kms-connector/crates/utils/src/types/solana_extra_data.rs (solana_user_decrypt_signing_message, Rust) and sdk/js-sdk/src/core/coprocessor/SolanaUserDecrypt-p.ts (solanaUserDecryptSigningMessage, TypeScript). Both implementations must produce message_utf8 byte-for-byte from input. commitment_hex is the pre-hash canonical request (sha256(commitment) is the 64-hex digest inside the message) so a diverging implementation can see WHERE its bytes drift, not only that they do. All hex is lowercase and unprefixed; all u64 fields are decimal strings (a JSON number would round-trip through IEEE-754 in a TypeScript consumer). These files are hand-committed literals, deliberately few: layout changes are forbidden without a new domain tag, so there is nothing to regenerate.",
